I search for the number and call the doctor's practice.
The phone only rings twice.
"Practice Doctor Schmidt, good morning," says the receptionist.
"What can I do for you?"
"Good morning, this is Maya Flores," I say quietly.
"I do not feel good at all today."
"I need an appointment, because I am sick."
"What is the matter with you?" she asks kindly.
"My head hurts and my throat hurts," I explain.
"And now my ears hurt too."
"Oh dear, that sounds like a heavy cold," says the receptionist.
"Are you already a patient with us?"
"Yes, I am," I answer and cough.
She types briefly on her keyboard.
"You should come by right away this morning," she says.
"We still have an appointment free at half past ten."
"Half past ten is good," I say relieved.
"Please bring your insurance card with you," she reminds me.
I thank her, hang up and get up slowly.
